<table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" bgcolor="#ffffff">
	<tr>
    <td>
<font face="Arial" size="+1"><B>Origin - UWOHoC After Chat for 8/30/2000</B></font>
		<p></p>

<font face=arial size=-1><br><b>&lt;Zauron&gt;</b> oh yeah, that's another thing I asked that didn't go through, are there going to be "interactive" emotes like shaking hands, kissing, hugging, etc?
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Not sure on the interactive emote question - the same stuff we use for combat flips should work, but no promises :)
<br>
<br><b>&lt;[KoW]Skipper[Cats]&gt;</b> How much will it cost?!
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> No promises on costs - not up to us dev types.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Danny5&gt;</b> Well I read a few previews and one said that you will be able to have upper body movement and lower body movement. Like when you are riding a horse you could slash at someone with a warhammer. Is this true ?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Danny5, yes and it works.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> You know that sliding you see in EQ when someone swings a sword?  Hopefully, you won't ever see that in UWOO
<br>
<br><b>&lt;drluvjoy1&gt;</b> I want to know if the dev team sits around after hours drinking beer, listening to punk music while laughing at the crazy gaming fans that spend all their waking hours following their game.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> drluvjoy&gt; depends on who you're talking about =)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> You have to remember, it's quite flattering to have fans.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;DruidLord&gt;</b> HEY UBIQ, i dont recall ..what exactly do u work on for uo2
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Druidlord, I'm the lead designer.  I design a lot of the systems, and manage the other designers 
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> At least he tries to manage us. :)
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Danny5&gt;</b> Ubiq: so far what do you think the system reqs will be ?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> SystemReqs&gt; too soon to say.  We want them as low as possible, so hopefully our graphics engine will be extremely scalable.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Shadowhand&gt;</b> Companions to help new players, think they should be in UO2? Why or why not?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Shadowhand&gt; I'd rather put in in-game incentives to recruit and help new players.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Aviak&gt;</b> heh,  Ok.  But i do need to know.  What are u guys doing to prevent economic ressession.  Commonly called "newbies that can afford plate"?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Aviak&gt; drains are the key.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Feydrex&gt;</b> Ubiq, do you have a college degree?  If so, which major?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Feydrex&gt; I'm an advertising major, perversely enough.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Shadowhand&gt;</b> Ubiq &gt; Not sure I followed that exactly, what do you mean by incentives to recruit and help new players?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Shadowhand&gt; similar to what AC did.  Make newbies valuable to high level players.  We aren't doing that same thing, but the concept is similar.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Therius&gt;</b> I'd like to see group spells.... 
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Therius&gt; planning on them, we'll see, but no promises.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Keebs_-GC-&gt;</b> Is overhead chat being explored/worked on or is it pretty much a no-go for ship?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Keebs&gt; we're still exploring, it's not an easy problem with the camera view we've planned.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Our engine is optimized to be at eye level.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Vernes&gt;</b> Ubiq: flying mounts?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Vernes&gt; not any time soon.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;RuneKnight&gt;</b> UBIQ Will you have allot of graphic detail I.E Ice on enchanted weapons or Colors or Fire resistant armor?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> RuneKnight&gt; We will do what we can.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> But not everything will have gfx effects.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;^noVa^&gt;</b> One thing that i like about UO is that i can run it in a window and be doing other things at the same time on my computer, would this even be possible in Origin?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> nova&gt; Depends on your video card.  Running windowed also will cause performance degredation.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;^noVa^&gt;</b> Ubiq is it possible to obtain a camera view that is similar to UO's
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Nova&gt; still experimenting.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Danny5&gt;</b> Ubiq: How would a 750 MhZ athalon with a GeForce 2 64 megs of RAM run in UWO ?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Danny5&gt;  Pretty damn good, I think.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Antitheus&gt;</b> I probably missed this, but for anyone that heard, UWO support HW T+L?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Antitheus&gt;  our lead graphics programmer is a big nVidia fan boy, expect us to use a lot of their features.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;[KoW]Skipper[Cats]&gt;</b> Are there the same diverse selections for clothes?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> SKipper&gt; there will be diverse clothing, but they won't be exactly the same.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Sparky619&gt;</b> what will our 10 ankhs buy? 1 box? 2?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> sparky&gt; most skills cost between 2 and 5 ankhs.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Tek_Yakuza&gt;</b> but how many ankhs do you get per level?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> tek&gt; that depends on the level.  You get 5 for the first few levels, 4 for the next ones, degrading down til you're getting 1 per level.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Meaning you hit the peak of your char around level 20-25.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;RuneKnight&gt;</b> UBIQ 1 last thing! Will your graphix engin SUPPORT FSAA and Open gl? 
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Runewizard&gt; I'm not really qualified to answer.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Crux&gt;</b> About how long do you plan for the casual player (less than 20 hours per week) to take to reach the initial level 50 cap?
