<br><b>&lt;Talebearer&gt;</b> supra, about the engine itself: Will characters be able to stand on one another like in Team Fortress Classic?
<br><b>&lt;supra&gt;</b> Yeah, characters don't collide with each-other, so you can pack a bunch of characters in the same space.
<br><b>&lt;supra&gt;</b> There's collision detection, but not between characters.
<br><b>&lt;Shadowhand&gt;</b> If there were collision detection between characters then you could, say, block off the only exit from a public building.
<br><b>&lt;supra&gt;</b> Exactly.  Plus detecting collision between two moving objects is a pretty expensive operation in terms of the amount of CPU it uses.
<br><b>&lt;supra&gt;</b> Basically, not having collision between players reduces the number of those checks we have to do, an prevents people from blocking.
<br><b>&lt;supra&gt;</b> Ubiq may have other reasons for not wanting collision between players that I'm not aware of as well.
<br><b>&lt;EolirinXianve&gt;</b> But there's collison with monsters and animals isn't there?
