<br><b>&lt;Kilgore&gt;</b> Ubiq, are you going to have a volenteer program (ala UO) or have it be more like the SB plan where the feature characters can't play the game and they are hired employees, having newbies rely on a guild for help?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Kilgore&gt; our system sounds like a hybrid.  The problem is that huge paid IGM/'feature character' staffs don't scale well economically.
<br><b>&lt;Kilgore&gt;</b> Ubiq, will you make the volenteer staff pretty much powerless?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Kilgore&gt; I plan to make them integral to the story.  Making them powerless wouldn't help that goal, would it?
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Aviak&gt;</b> When fighting.  Will the things that you fight react to your moves?  Like falling back?  Or will they just stand there and take a drop in Hp?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Aviak, to some degree our characters are reactive, but there are some issues with latency that prevent the perfect response you expect from, say, quake
<br><b>&lt;Aviak&gt;</b> Cause when that guy was swinging at the orc, that thing wasen't reacting to anyone, just taking it's occational swing.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Aviak&gt; we're working on that pretty much right now =)
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Zauron&gt;</b> I think the system of each level gives less ankhs to spend, thereby decreasing the difference in power once you get past a certain level, will help alleviate the problems with the over-focus on leveling that plagues EQ
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Zauron&gt; one of the larger contributors to the 'must level' feel is the fact that you can't group with people far above you.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Aviak&gt;</b> What about EAX?
<br><b>&lt;supra&gt;</b> Aviak - the Origin audio system is based off the U9 audio system, which used EAX.  It's been greatly improved as well.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Kilgore&gt;</b> Ubiq, Well UO2 be constantly added to or big enough so that you can never explore it all? Some of the funest times I had in UO were as a very young player adventuring with a friend, however there weren't many places to go.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Kilgore&gt; we have the ability to add to the world dynamically.  Whether or not we do will be up to the priorities set by the fans and the live team.
<br><b>&lt;supra&gt;</b> Kilgore - The landmass of Origin is MUCH larger than that of UO.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Storyline pace&gt; it will be reasonable, but slow enough so you won't fall behind if you log off a month.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Each 'chapter' needs enough time to touch everyone before you move to the next chapter.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Zauron&gt;</b> Ubiq&gt; Did you come up with that or someone else on your team?  'CAuse whoever did really had a fantastic idea
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Zauron, that was me.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;NetDogma&gt;</b> Ubiq&gt; When is your best guess as to the release date of UWOO? Are you guys looking to possibly push it back, in the spirit of Diablo II, or are you not allowed to comment on that sort of thing? (sorry for asking, I know you've heard this one a lot)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> NO comments on the date.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;EolirinXianve&gt;</b> ubiq, hoods? 
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Eol&gt; Maybe.
<br>
<br><b>&lt;Ghosty&gt;</b> Ubiq, is the movie in the making right now
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> I have no idea what the status of the Anime is. 
<br>
<br><b>&lt;I-Watcher&gt;</b> say Ubiq will there be underwater exploration
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> We are focusing most of our energies on the overland world.



</font>

</td></tr></table>

